{"authored" [{"question" "q-8063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{4}=2,\\,b=\\sqrt{16}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{4}{2}x \\\\  & =\\pm 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "categor