$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{6},\\,b=\\sqrt{24}=2\\sqrt{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{6}}x \\\\  & =\\pm 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-116551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-116551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-116551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm 2x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-116551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm 4x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-116551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-116551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-116551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}=1$ are$\\,\\,y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{16}=4,\\,b=\\sqrt{36}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{4}{6}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "5342120630873a37658f88db0eab6edd645319cbe5ec7bbc35fce11c63be16c2" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{36} - \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-7426.json" "file_sha256" "5d71748f6b1f177ed65bf13153afef1c044de51fb98d0ad1b8050ef1b9a87631" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{36} = 6, \\qquad b=\\sqrt9 =3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{6}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-7426.json" "file_sha256" "5d71748f6b1f177ed65bf13153afef1c044de51fb98d0ad1b8050ef1b9a87631" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{y^2}{9} - \\dfrac{x^2}{16} = 1$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-5356.json" "file_sha256" "25b040ee46832290d03bb484b7bfd4d047c941cb3face9310434bdb6c6f3c527" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{y^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{x^2}{b^2} = 1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{a}{b} x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{9} = 3, \\qquad b=\\sqrt{16} = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y = \\pm \\dfrac{3}{4}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-5356.json" "file_sha256" "25b040ee46832290d03bb484b7bfd4d047c941cb3face9310434bdb6c6f3c527" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $25 x ^ 2 - 9 y ^ 2 = 225$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-5357.json" "file_sha256" "ad7390d334eda1212106cbed5c0e778997bd5b7318b551c86d65463d0a921b12" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $225$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =225 \\\\ \\frac{25{x}^{2}}{225}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{225} & =\\frac{225}{225} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt 9 = 3,$ and $b=\\sqrt{25} = 5.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\dfrac{5}{3}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-5357.json" "file_sha256" "ad7390d334eda1212106cbed5c0e778997bd5b7318b551c86d65463d0a921b12" "basis" 1777 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-116549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{2},\\,b=\\sqrt{25}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eed75569b01102438865dcc54eba711ff91acc736cc07f6f34ca9e3749c5954a"} {"question" "q-116549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-8063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asy