e hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}x \\\\  & =\\pm 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eed75569b01102438865dcc54eba711ff91acc736cc07f6f34ca9e3749c5954a"} {"question" "q-116560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm 2x"] ["math" "y=\\pm 4x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116560" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm 2x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{25}=5,\\,b=\\sqrt{9}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{3}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eed75569b01102438865dcc54eba711ff91acc736cc07f6f34ca9e3749c5954a"} {"question" "q-10433" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10433" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{25}{9}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{3}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{9}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{9}{5}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10433" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{3}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{3},\\,b=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eed75569b01102438865dcc54eba711ff91acc736cc07f6f34ca9e3749c5954a"} {"question" "q-116559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm 2x"] ["math" "y=\\pm 4x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-116559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $25{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}=400.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $400$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{25{y}^{2}}{400}-\\frac{16{x}^{2}}{400} & =\\frac{400}{400} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{16}=4$ and $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eed75569b01102438865dcc54eba711ff91acc736cc07f6f34ca9e3749c5954a"} {"question" "q-10441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{4}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-10441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-7976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $3{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-7976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $12$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{12} & =\\frac{12}{12} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{4}=2,$ and $b=\\sqrt{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-7976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eed75569b01102438865dcc54eba711ff91acc736cc07f6f34ca9e3749c5954a"} {"question" "q-7976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-7976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-7976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-316956" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The asymptotes of the hyperbola $18{y}^{2}-50{x}^{2}=900$ are$\\,\\,y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-316956" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $900$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18{y}^{2}-50{x}^{2} & =900 \\\\ \\frac{18{y}^{2}}{900}-\\frac{50{x}^{2}}{900} & =\\frac{900}{900} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{50}=5\\sqrt{2}$ and $b=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{50}}{\\sqrt{18}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-316956" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eed75569b01102438865dcc54eba711ff91acc736cc07f6f34ca9e3749c5954a"} {"question" "q-316956" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-316956" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{3}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-316951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The asymptotes of the hyperbola $4{y}^{2}-9{x}^{2}=36$ are$\\,\\,y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-316951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $36$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-9{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36} & =\\frac{36}{36} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{9}=3$ and $b=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-316951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eed75569b01102438865dcc54eba711ff91acc736cc07f6f34ca9e3749c5954a"} {"question" "q-316951" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-316951" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-275216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The asymptotes of the hyperbola $2{x}^{2}-18{y}^{2}=162$ are$\\,\\,y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-275216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $162$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-18{y}^{2} & =162 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{162}-\\frac{18{y}^{2}}{162} & =\\frac{162}{162} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{81}=9,$ and $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{9}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-275216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eed75569b01102438865dcc54eba711ff91acc736cc07f6f34ca9e3749c5954a"} {"question" "q-275216" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "q-275216" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c40954da2f9101cf7f14a8e98e63ae50fa72e99e3dba7f33d0aea78b902d432"} {"question" "e-7426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{36} - \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/example-7426.json" "file_sha256" "5d71748f6b1f177ed65bf13153afef1c044de51fb98d0ad1b8050ef1b9a87631"} {"question" "e-7426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{36} = 6, \\qquad b=\\sqrt9 =3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{6}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/example-7426.json" "file_sha256" "5d71748f6b1f177ed65bf13153afef1c044de51fb98d0ad1b8050ef1b9a87631"} {"question" "e-5356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{y^2}{9} - \\dfrac{x^2}{16} = 1$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/example-5356.json" "file_sha256" "25b040ee46832290d03bb484b7bfd4d047c941cb3face9310434bdb6c6f3c527"} {"question" "e-5356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{y^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{x^2}{b^2} = 1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{a}{b} x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{9} = 3, \\qquad b=\\sqrt{16} = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y = \\pm \\dfrac{3}{4}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/example-5356.json" "file_sha256" "25b040ee46832290d03bb484b7bfd4d047c941cb3face9310434bdb6c6f3c527"} {"question" "e-5357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $25 x ^ 2 - 9 y ^ 2 = 225$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/example-5357.json" "file_sha256" "ad7390d334eda1212106cbed5c0e778997bd5b7318b551c86d65463d0a921b12"} {"question" "e-5357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $225$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =225 \\\\ \\frac{25{x}^{2}}{225}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{225} & =\\frac{225}{225} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt 9 = 3,$ and $b=\\sqrt{25} = 5.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\dfrac{5}{3}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076822/example-5357.json" "file_sha256" "ad7390d334eda1212106cbed5c0e778997bd5b7318b551c86d65463d0a921b12"}] "usage" {"q-10433" [] "e-7426" [] "q-116551" [] "e-5357" [] "q-316965" [] "q-8063" [] "e-5356" []} "basis" 2785 "retractions" [[17592186087913 :question/problem "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{y^{2}}{25} - \\frac{x^{2}}{9} = 1$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186084490 17592186084491 17592186084492 17592186084493 17592186084494 17592186330598 17592186330599 17592186330600 17592186330601 17592186330602 17592186330635 17592186330652 17592186330653 17592186330654 17592186330655 17592186330656] "immutable_fields" [[17592186084489 :answer-field/correct] [17592186084489 :answer-field/id] [17592186084489 :answer-field/key] [17592186084489 :answer-field/type] [17592186330597 :answer-field/correct] [17592186330597 :answer-field/id] [17592186330597 :answer-field/key] [17592186330597 :answer-field/type] [17592186330634 :answer-field/correct] [17592186330634 :answer-field/id] [17592186330634 :answer-field/key] [17592186330634 :answer-field/type] [17592186330651 :answer-field/correct] [17592186330651 :answer-field/id] [17592186330651 :answer-field/key] [17592186330651 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
